WEBVTT

00:22.272 --> 00:24.412
Well, we managed to seal it.

00:24.412 --> 00:26.572
That should stop the culling for now,

00:26.922 --> 00:29.072
but it's only a matter of time.

00:29.592 --> 00:31.752
Unless the Demon King is defeated,

00:31.752 --> 00:35.582
the world will eventually be swallowed up
by the reverse dungeon Tenebre.

00:36.102 --> 00:38.212
Just like my nephew's homeland.

00:41.032 --> 00:42.712
Why are you all so discouraged?

00:44.022 --> 00:46.302
I'm not discouraged at all.

00:46.302 --> 00:48.042
In fact, I'm hopeful.

00:48.582 --> 00:53.472
Someday, someone will carry on
our will and save the world.

00:54.092 --> 00:57.772
Yes, someday, a new hero will appear.

00:58.792 --> 01:00.232
Physical Enchant!

01:00.482 --> 01:02.822
(Enhanced Stamina, Enhanced Arm Strength,
Enhanced Leg Strength)

01:06.722 --> 01:08.612
Scroll of Light Shield!

01:09.112 --> 01:10.480
(Scroll of Light Shield)

01:10.492 --> 01:14.230
- Raging hellfire, burn the evil ones to ash!
- Our God in heaven, great one
who rules the heavens...

01:15.522 --> 01:18.872
Grade 3 Magic: Jet Fire!

01:20.772 --> 01:23.252
Enchant Weapon: Flame Scratch!

01:24.002 --> 01:25.512
(Enchant Weapon)
(Flame Scratch)

01:25.512 --> 01:26.882
This will end it!

01:32.282 --> 01:35.102
That's the A-rank party,
Thunder Pike, for you!

01:35.452 --> 01:38.032
They took down the nasty
Hydra with no problem!

01:38.032 --> 01:40.072
Their individual strengths are incredible,

01:40.072 --> 01:43.042
but above all, their teamwork
as a party is god-tier!

01:43.042 --> 01:46.362
They're living up to their A-rank status!

01:46.692 --> 01:50.232
And their live stream has drawn
over one million viewers!

01:50.232 --> 01:52.882
Their popularity is through the roof!

01:52.882 --> 01:55.860
Can't wait to see where
this party goes from here!

01:55.860 --> 01:55.872
- Thunder Pike! Thunder Pike! Thunder Pike!

01:55.872 --> 01:58.072
- That's Thunder Pike for you!
- Thunder Pike! Thunder Pike! Thunder Pike!

01:58.072 --> 02:00.652
- We gotta hurry up and get to their level, too!
- Thunder Pike! Thunder Pike! Thunder Pike!

02:00.652 --> 02:03.142
- Simon is so hot!
- Thunder Pike! Thunder Pike! Thunder Pike!

02:03.142 --> 02:03.950
- Thunder Pike! Thunder Pike! Thunder Pike!

02:08.882 --> 02:09.710
As of today, I'm leaving Thunder Pike!

02:09.710 --> 02:13.210
(Red Mage / Alchemist, Yuke Score: B-rank)
As of today, I'm leaving Thunder Pike!

02:14.470 --> 02:15.900
(Leader of Thunder Pike)
Mind telling us why, Yuke?

02:15.900 --> 02:17.460
( Knight Simon Score: A-rank)
Mind telling us why, Yuke?

02:17.472 --> 02:20.452
I don't think our compensation
is being divided up fairly.

02:20.452 --> 02:21.732
I've said this over and over.

02:21.732 --> 02:24.482
My cut from today's quest
is pathetic, too.

02:24.482 --> 02:26.052
I'll go into debt at this rate!

02:26.052 --> 02:30.352
Adventurers like us may belong to
parties, but we're still individuals.

02:30.352 --> 02:33.730
Of course compensation is going to be
adjusted depending on one's contribution.

02:33.730 --> 02:35.222
(Warrior, Barry Score: A-rank)

02:35.222 --> 02:37.102
(Warrior, Barry Score: A-rank)
You don't even fight.

02:37.102 --> 02:39.252
You just burn through all our items.

02:39.572 --> 02:40.882
"Burn through"?

02:40.882 --> 02:43.990
Shouldn't you be grateful
we give you a cut at all?

02:43.990 --> 02:44.352
(Witch, Jamie Score: A-rank)

02:44.352 --> 02:47.762
(Witch, Jamie Score: A-rank)
I think he's only useful when
we're prepping our streams.

02:47.762 --> 02:48.692
(Witch, Jamie Score: A-rank)
Come on, Jamie!

02:48.692 --> 02:52.512
I mean, I can't use the streaming
artifact myself, but...

02:52.512 --> 02:52.882
(Priestess, Camilla Score: A-rank)

02:52.882 --> 02:57.880
(Priestess, Camilla Score: A-rank)
If you want reasonable pay, you need
to make a reasonable contribution.

02:58.592 --> 03:01.562
You say that like it's a sound argument,

03:01.562 --> 03:05.152
but I'm pretty sure you receive more
of my support than anyone else!

03:05.762 --> 03:09.032
I haven't the faintest idea what you mean.

03:09.032 --> 03:11.212
It's because I help out
with magic and items—

03:11.212 --> 03:13.572
What are you gonna do once you leave us?

03:13.572 --> 03:15.662
You'll never get by in any other party.

03:16.302 --> 03:20.682
You're only B-rank now because your
childhood friend did you a favor,

03:20.682 --> 03:25.042
and yet we're letting you be in
our A-rank party, Thunder Pike.

03:25.742 --> 03:28.542
So you're saying you'll
be just fine without me?

03:29.072 --> 03:31.452
Hey, so you do get it.

03:31.452 --> 03:33.932
No one's gonna suffer
if you're not around.

03:34.232 --> 03:36.922
Well, then, I'm quitting.

03:36.922 --> 03:38.302
Thanks for the past five years!

03:38.722 --> 03:41.492
No... I'm the one who's
been taking care of you!

03:41.492 --> 03:43.062
You should be thanking me!

03:43.062 --> 03:44.662
You can come crying back,

03:44.662 --> 03:47.312
but there won't be a place
for you here anymore!

03:47.852 --> 03:50.442
I wish you the best. Farewell.

03:50.802 --> 03:52.852
You sure that's what you want?

03:52.852 --> 03:55.572
There's still time to say you're joking.

03:59.752 --> 04:01.042
I won't put up with this!

04:09.160 --> 04:16.120
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

05:31.002 --> 05:35.002
(The Adventure City Finis)

05:36.012 --> 05:40.500
(Episode 1: Clover Is Born)

05:40.500 --> 05:42.090
(Episode 1: Clover Is Born)
Yeah, that's it!

05:42.512 --> 05:44.002
You've got this!

05:45.602 --> 05:48.522
I sure could use some new gear.

05:52.010 --> 05:52.552
(Receptionist Mamar)

05:52.552 --> 05:54.760
(Receptionist Mamar)
Good morning, Yuke.

05:54.772 --> 05:58.032
I'm, uh... here to sign up for new work.

05:58.452 --> 06:00.042
For new work?

06:00.042 --> 06:02.532
What happened to Thunder Pike?

06:02.532 --> 06:05.232
I left the party yesterday.

06:05.232 --> 06:09.042
Oh, my... Well, I suppose
a lot can happen in five years.

06:09.632 --> 06:13.092
All right, please fill out this form.

06:14.292 --> 06:16.522
Name: Yuke Feldio.

06:16.522 --> 06:18.072
(Name: Yuke Feldio)
Age: 20.

06:18.072 --> 06:18.960
- Sex: male.

06:18.960 --> 06:19.442
- You still have such lovely handwriting.
- Sex: male.

06:19.442 --> 06:21.552
- You still have such lovely handwriting.
- Job: Red Mage and Alchemist.

06:22.092 --> 06:25.712
Alchemy requires precise penmanship.

06:25.712 --> 06:28.810
- Impressive. I'll have this posted on the—

06:28.810 --> 06:29.920
- Master!
- Impressive. I'll have this posted on the—

06:31.432 --> 06:33.672
It's been ages, Master!

06:33.672 --> 06:35.522
Y-You're Marina, right?

06:35.962 --> 06:37.430
Yes! I'm Marina!

06:37.430 --> 06:37.872
(Sword Mage Marina)
Yes! I'm Marina!

06:37.872 --> 06:41.020
(Sword Mage Marina)
Thanks for your instructions during
Adventurer Preliminary Training!

06:41.032 --> 06:42.792
It's been half a year.

06:42.792 --> 06:44.482
Is everyone still all right?

06:44.482 --> 06:47.302
Yeah! Silk and Rain are doing great, too!

06:47.302 --> 06:48.542
Glad to hear it.

06:48.542 --> 06:50.492
So what were you doing?

06:50.492 --> 06:52.302
Uh, I'm looking for a party.

06:52.302 --> 06:54.242
Huh? You're on the market?!

06:55.402 --> 06:58.672
Then why don't you join our party?

07:00.892 --> 07:01.790
So in other words,

07:01.790 --> 07:02.112
(Ranger / Elemental Silk)

07:02.112 --> 07:05.292
(Ranger / Elemental Silk)
you want to join our party?

07:05.292 --> 07:07.040
(Ranger / Elemental Silk)
Do I have that right?

07:07.382 --> 07:09.062
Yeah... I guess so.

07:09.442 --> 07:12.692
We can let Master in,
right, Rain? Silk?

07:13.192 --> 07:16.050
(Priestess / Mage Rain)
Yeah. I think it's fine.

07:16.352 --> 07:18.732
I won't oppose it, either...

07:19.282 --> 07:21.522
but are you sure, Master?

07:21.522 --> 07:24.322
We're a D-rank party
that's just starting out.

07:24.852 --> 07:30.252
As a B-rank adventurer, you wouldn't
gain much from it, would you?

07:30.252 --> 07:32.242
That's not a problem.

07:32.242 --> 07:35.082
I think that suits me better, anyway.

07:35.542 --> 07:37.082
What do you mean?

07:37.082 --> 07:41.592
A-rank parties take on really
high-level quests and dungeons.

07:41.592 --> 07:45.052
With the cost of the items I went
through, I was constantly in debt.

07:45.052 --> 07:48.212
So low-ranked, oh, sorry!

07:48.212 --> 07:50.162
Oh, it's all right.

07:50.162 --> 07:54.352
D-rank quests should offer a better
balance of cost and compensation.

07:54.832 --> 07:55.982
I see.

07:56.402 --> 07:58.862
So it's okay, right? That settles it!

07:58.862 --> 08:00.782
Yes, Master.

08:00.782 --> 08:02.492
Very well, Master.

08:02.492 --> 08:04.812
Oh, please don't call me that.

08:04.812 --> 08:07.972
You can just call me Yuke from now on.

08:07.972 --> 08:10.372
Okay! Glad to have you with us, Yuke!

08:10.762 --> 08:14.222
It is a pleasure, Yuke... sir.

08:14.222 --> 08:16.872
Welcome, Yuke.

08:17.242 --> 08:18.862
Thanks. Glad to be here.

08:19.342 --> 08:22.382
It's been ages since I felt like this...

08:22.722 --> 08:25.202
So, what shall we do today?

08:25.202 --> 08:26.512
Do you have plans?

08:26.512 --> 08:28.920
We've accepted a quest to collect

08:28.932 --> 08:31.902
(Paintal Abandoned Mine Dungeon)
magic iron ore from the Paintal
Abandoned Mine Dungeon.

08:31.902 --> 08:32.420
(Paintal Abandoned Mine Dungeon)

08:36.352 --> 08:37.982
It's been so long.

08:39.012 --> 08:39.982
As I recall,

08:39.982 --> 08:44.242
there are several spots on the sixth floor of
this dungeon where you can mine magic iron ore.

08:44.242 --> 08:48.402
Yes, but... we don't want to
fight the fifth-floor boss,

08:48.402 --> 08:51.992
so we were hoping there'd be
a way to mine it before that.

08:52.832 --> 08:55.562
We should start on the fourth floor, then.

08:55.562 --> 08:58.002
Okay, girls, let's have fun,
but be careful.

09:03.712 --> 09:06.062
They're doing everything
just the way I taught them.

09:06.722 --> 09:08.132
But for now...

09:08.672 --> 09:10.882
Marina, I'll take the lead.

09:10.882 --> 09:13.392
Huh? But you're a Red Mage, right?

09:13.772 --> 09:16.522
I thought if a party didn't
have a Thief or Scout,

09:16.522 --> 09:20.022
its toughest Sword Mage was
supposed to take the lead.

09:20.402 --> 09:21.772
Generally, yes...

09:21.772 --> 09:22.722
(Detecting Lantern)

09:22.722 --> 09:26.020
(Detecting Lantern)
but for a poor guy, I happen
to be quite resourceful.

09:27.532 --> 09:29.722
What's that? It's so pretty!

09:29.722 --> 09:32.162
It's an artifact called
a Detecting Lantern.

09:32.832 --> 09:34.662
It uses a special type of oil.

09:34.962 --> 09:39.292
With this, we can find traps as
easily as an experienced Thief.

09:39.632 --> 09:40.912
That's so awesome!

09:40.912 --> 09:42.172
Wow...

09:42.172 --> 09:45.052
A special oil? Isn't that expensive?

09:45.312 --> 09:47.012
Don't worry.

09:47.012 --> 09:49.932
I made this oil using alchemy.

09:50.322 --> 09:51.982
I'll take the lead.

09:51.982 --> 09:54.942
Marina, you take the rear and
be ready for any ambushes.

09:54.942 --> 09:55.562
Right!

09:58.642 --> 10:00.202
Watch out over there.

10:00.202 --> 10:01.562
O-Okay...

10:01.562 --> 10:03.162
Marina, can you see?

10:03.162 --> 10:05.322
Perfectly! No worries!

10:07.762 --> 10:11.862
This was the first dungeon
Thunder Pike went into, too.

10:15.742 --> 10:16.992
Stop!

10:17.592 --> 10:20.532
There's something in the small
chamber 20 yards ahead.

10:20.532 --> 10:21.822
Prepare to fight.

10:29.000 --> 10:29.432
(Bogles)

10:29.432 --> 10:30.682
(Bogles)
They're Bogles!

10:30.682 --> 10:32.000
(Bogles)

10:32.432 --> 10:33.512
I'll take initiative!

10:36.762 --> 10:38.102
I'll handle the rest!

10:38.482 --> 10:39.732
Physical Enchant!

10:41.732 --> 10:43.482
(Enhanced Stamina, Enhanced Arm Strength,
Enhanced Leg Strength)

10:43.482 --> 10:44.982
Snare!

10:45.982 --> 10:47.232
(Snare)

10:48.482 --> 10:50.072
Marina, now!

10:55.422 --> 10:56.662
Well done.

10:57.122 --> 11:00.912
That was... your magic, wasn't it?

11:01.242 --> 11:04.692
Yeah. I cast three types
of Physical Enchant on you.

11:04.692 --> 11:07.362
What? Three at the same time?

11:07.362 --> 11:10.552
And that was a quick cast
with no incantation!

11:11.102 --> 11:14.562
I feel so much lighter!
That was super easy!

11:14.562 --> 11:16.342
You're the one who did it all.

11:16.342 --> 11:17.612
You've gotten stronger.

11:17.612 --> 11:20.562
Okay, let's get some ore and keep moving.

11:25.492 --> 11:28.022
What's your dungeon attack routine like?

11:28.022 --> 11:29.362
Rest after each floor?

11:29.692 --> 11:32.872
Yeah. We report our losses regularly, too.

11:32.872 --> 11:34.612
Another thing we learned from you!

11:35.112 --> 11:37.442
We remain faithful to the basics.

11:37.442 --> 11:38.772
Good.

11:38.772 --> 11:41.622
Let's rest a bit, then continue down.

11:43.862 --> 11:46.232
No damage to my weapons or armor.

11:46.232 --> 11:47.632
Plenty of strength left, too!

11:47.632 --> 11:50.172
I've retrieved the arrows I used.

11:50.172 --> 11:51.602
No losses here.

11:51.602 --> 11:53.632
No losses for me, either.

11:53.942 --> 11:56.142
Practically nothing lost for me, as well.

11:56.142 --> 11:57.512
And plenty of mana.

11:57.512 --> 12:01.022
(Second Floor)

12:11.122 --> 12:11.890
Dead miners! Lots of them!

12:11.890 --> 12:13.442
(Dead Miners)
Dead miners! Lots of them!

12:13.442 --> 12:14.520
(Dead Miners)

12:14.972 --> 12:15.652
Rain!

12:18.272 --> 12:20.412
Our God in heaven...

12:20.412 --> 12:22.372
Marina! Master! Cover me!

12:22.372 --> 12:23.542
Okay!

12:23.882 --> 12:25.172
Leave this to me.

12:25.172 --> 12:27.042
Protection! Little Blessing!

12:27.672 --> 12:30.042
(Protection)
(Little Blessing)

12:32.552 --> 12:34.302
The undead aren't coming near us!

12:36.602 --> 12:39.502
Guide them to peace in the heavens above.

12:39.502 --> 12:40.812
Turn Undead!

12:47.342 --> 12:49.172
Way to go, Rain!

12:49.172 --> 12:51.732
You bought me time.

12:52.072 --> 12:53.362
You saved us!

12:53.662 --> 12:57.852
Not many people can use
Turn Undead on that scale.

12:57.852 --> 12:59.872
It probably consumed a lot of mana.

13:00.392 --> 13:01.372
Refresh Mana.

13:01.372 --> 13:02.132
(Refresh Mana)

13:02.132 --> 13:02.860
(Refresh Mana)
Refresh Mana?

13:02.860 --> 13:03.672
Refresh Mana?

13:04.242 --> 13:06.372
You can use Refresh Mana?

13:06.722 --> 13:08.952
What? Is that a really strong spell?

13:08.952 --> 13:10.452
Yeah, very.

13:10.452 --> 13:14.012
It's an extremely rare spell
that only Red Mages can use.

13:14.012 --> 13:16.882
Just being able to use it can
get you into A-rank parties.

13:16.882 --> 13:18.162
Wow!

13:18.162 --> 13:19.792
I never knew that!

13:19.792 --> 13:21.512
That's a bit of an exaggeration.

13:21.982 --> 13:24.082
Red Mage is a pretty obscure job,

13:24.082 --> 13:26.272
so I've learned a few tricks
to compensate.

13:26.592 --> 13:29.902
It wasn't easy to
get the grimoire, though.

13:33.522 --> 13:35.892
What are you doing now?

13:35.892 --> 13:38.802
Pouring holy water over
the undead's footprints.

13:38.802 --> 13:42.012
It's an easy way to keep them
from pursuing or flanking us.

13:42.012 --> 13:44.162
Isn't that expensive, too?

13:44.552 --> 13:46.262
If you buy it, sure.

13:46.262 --> 13:49.162
But I made this myself, too,
so don't worry.

13:49.162 --> 13:50.962
You made your own holy water?!

13:50.962 --> 13:52.922
But you're not even a priest...

13:52.922 --> 13:54.722
Aside from the usual methods,

13:54.722 --> 13:56.832
I can make it from the purifying ash that

13:56.832 --> 13:58.802
undead leave behind after you defeat them.

13:59.122 --> 14:00.802
Is that also alchemy?

14:01.082 --> 14:04.022
It's what they call a secret recipe.

14:04.022 --> 14:05.662
The ash we got from those dead miners

14:05.662 --> 14:08.182
was more than enough to make
up for the amount I'm using.

14:08.182 --> 14:09.842
I see!

14:09.842 --> 14:13.192
High-ranked adventurers really do
have experience on another level!

14:13.572 --> 14:16.322
You're welcome to learn
whatever you can from me.

14:16.632 --> 14:19.812
Of course! Please teach us
lots of things, Master!

14:19.812 --> 14:20.532
Yeah.

14:23.002 --> 14:26.522
From this point on, we'll be looking
for spots to mine for magic iron ore,

14:26.522 --> 14:28.202
so let's stop to refuel here.

14:28.722 --> 14:31.332
Sit tight. I'll whip something up.

14:34.922 --> 14:37.592
O-Oh! A Magic Bag!

14:37.982 --> 14:39.592
Is this your first time seeing one?

14:39.592 --> 14:41.222
This wasn't cheap, you know.

14:41.842 --> 14:43.092
I'd like to have one someday.

14:43.572 --> 14:46.852
Keep adventuring, and you'll
have your chance to get one.

14:46.852 --> 14:49.482
They aren't that rare or anything.

14:52.642 --> 14:54.482
Watch closely, you three.

15:02.002 --> 15:04.552
Mm, smells good.

15:04.552 --> 15:06.492
It's seafood soup today.

15:06.872 --> 15:10.832
What is this? What is this?
Amazing! Amazing!

15:10.832 --> 15:13.372
I see you're still an artifact freak.

15:13.932 --> 15:16.120
I found this in the Aureus
Royal Castle Ruins Dungeon.

15:16.120 --> 15:16.882
(Soup Stock)
I found this in the Aureus
Royal Castle Ruins Dungeon.

15:16.882 --> 15:18.870
(Soup Stock)
It's a magic pot called Soup Stock.

15:19.252 --> 15:22.112
It sure cost a lot to
have it repaired, though.

15:22.112 --> 15:23.262
Pretty cool, isn't it?

15:23.852 --> 15:25.832
It's incredibly interesting!

15:25.832 --> 15:28.292
I never knew such an artifact existed!

15:29.382 --> 15:33.592
I'm so hungry! I can't take it anymore!

15:33.592 --> 15:35.652
Come, now. That's so improper.

15:37.822 --> 15:39.372
I can't believe it!

15:39.372 --> 15:42.782
We actually get to eat a
decent meal in a dungeon!

15:43.052 --> 15:45.662
Go on, eat up while it's hot.

15:45.982 --> 15:47.412
Don't mind if I do!

15:48.182 --> 15:49.162
Let's eat.

15:51.472 --> 15:52.542
It's good!

15:57.602 --> 16:00.062
It's so warm... and so good!

16:00.062 --> 16:02.172
Yes, it really is delicious!

16:07.432 --> 16:11.682
Master, I feel as if this
food is enveloped in mana.

16:12.052 --> 16:14.612
Your mana detection
is as keen as ever, huh?

16:14.612 --> 16:16.192
What does it mean?

16:16.192 --> 16:21.152
Well... in a broad sense, cooking is
basically a form of alchemy, right?

16:21.152 --> 16:22.442
No, it isn't...

16:22.442 --> 16:24.612
Since we'll be mining after this,

16:24.612 --> 16:27.312
I packed it with some extra
love to keep your strength up

16:27.312 --> 16:28.952
so you won't get tired.

16:28.952 --> 16:31.972
Wait... Cooking is made with love?

16:31.972 --> 16:34.242
Love is... mana?

16:34.242 --> 16:36.322
Silk, don't think about it.

16:36.322 --> 16:37.712
Just go with how it feels.

16:37.712 --> 16:40.462
Whatever, let's just eat! It's good!

16:42.712 --> 16:46.472
(Fourth Floor)

16:46.472 --> 16:48.972
(Rock Lizard)

16:49.312 --> 16:52.102
This mining spot is pretty impressive.

16:52.722 --> 16:54.852
We should be able to get
lots of magic iron ore.

16:56.482 --> 16:57.352
Slow!

16:57.852 --> 16:59.352
(Slow)

16:59.822 --> 17:01.942
It's as if time just stopped!

17:02.382 --> 17:03.322
Here I go!

17:03.602 --> 17:04.722
Magic Blade!

17:05.572 --> 17:07.992
I feel so light! I should be able to...

17:22.532 --> 17:26.522
Magic Blade uses a ton
of strength and mana...

17:27.442 --> 17:30.582
I can only keep it up
for about ten seconds.

17:30.582 --> 17:33.852
Just keep using the ability,
and you'll get used to it.

17:34.572 --> 17:35.802
Refresh Mana.

17:42.100 --> 17:42.672
(Wrecking Pickaxe)

17:42.672 --> 17:44.720
(Wrecking Pickaxe)
Well, let's get digging.

17:47.362 --> 17:50.312
Master, please allow us to help, too.

17:50.312 --> 17:53.642
In that case, you can gather
the bits of ore that fall.

17:53.642 --> 17:54.832
Got it.

17:56.372 --> 17:58.882
Okay, that should do it.

17:58.882 --> 18:01.002
How much ore do you need?

18:01.002 --> 18:04.492
Twenty standard ingots, so...

18:04.492 --> 18:06.002
Just a little bit more.

18:06.952 --> 18:08.882
So we'll need to defeat one more...

18:10.622 --> 18:12.002
Here's a thought.

18:12.002 --> 18:15.262
Why don't we defeat the floor
boss and head to the sixth floor?

18:16.152 --> 18:20.002
But the floor boss is the Steel Crab!
It's nicknamed the "Novice Slayer"!

18:20.002 --> 18:23.502
It's tougher than a Rock Lizard,
so you need powerful magic.

18:23.502 --> 18:26.022
I don't think I can cut through it!

18:26.312 --> 18:30.162
Don't worry. I'll take on the
floor boss with all I've got.

18:30.162 --> 18:33.662
I've gotta show you guys that
I can be useful, after all.

18:33.952 --> 18:36.772
We've already seen quite
clearly how amazing you are!

18:36.772 --> 18:39.052
She's right! You blew us away!

18:39.052 --> 18:39.662
Yeah.

18:39.662 --> 18:41.362
Did I?

18:41.362 --> 18:44.172
But there's still lots more I can do.

18:44.172 --> 18:48.172
(Fifth Floor)

18:48.692 --> 18:51.902
So the floor boss is just ahead,

18:51.902 --> 18:53.662
but I'll fight alone this time.

18:53.662 --> 18:56.322
What? Are you gonna be okay, Yuke?

18:56.322 --> 18:57.932
I told you, I'll be fine.

18:57.932 --> 18:59.430
(Floating Automatic Recording Artifact, Camerat)

18:59.430 --> 19:01.030
Camerat...

19:01.212 --> 19:02.952
A Camerat...

19:02.952 --> 19:04.442
You're going to stream it?

19:04.732 --> 19:06.112
No, just record it.

19:06.112 --> 19:09.322
I record all my floor boss battles.

19:11.072 --> 19:14.262
Hey, Yuke, let's livestream this!

19:14.262 --> 19:16.582
Sure, but... why?

19:16.582 --> 19:18.082
'Cause it seems like fun!

19:19.772 --> 19:20.832
Guess I will, then.

19:21.312 --> 19:25.052
Wait, I just realized I never
asked your party's name.

19:25.052 --> 19:26.342
What do you call yourselves?

19:26.652 --> 19:29.212
I'm embarrassed to say
we don't have a name yet.

19:29.212 --> 19:31.972
We haven't even officially
registered as a party.

19:32.292 --> 19:33.972
So let's pick one now!

19:33.972 --> 19:35.512
Do you have a good idea for one?

19:35.512 --> 19:38.252
W-Well...

19:38.252 --> 19:40.182
Haven't thought about it at all, eh?

19:41.562 --> 19:42.732
Clover!

19:43.132 --> 19:44.232
Clover?

19:44.582 --> 19:45.792
One leaf,

19:45.792 --> 19:46.482
two leaves,

19:46.922 --> 19:47.862
three leaves...

19:48.262 --> 19:51.052
and you're our lucky fourth leaf!

19:51.052 --> 19:52.112
Lucky?

19:52.712 --> 19:53.992
What do you think?

19:54.402 --> 19:55.762
It's a lovely name.

19:55.762 --> 19:57.742
Yeah. I like it.

20:00.232 --> 20:01.522
Okay, then.

20:01.522 --> 20:04.742
When we get back, we'll register as
a party at the Adventurer's Guild.

20:04.742 --> 20:06.382
We are Clover!

20:06.382 --> 20:08.502
Yeah! Clover!

20:08.862 --> 20:10.002
Clover!

20:10.432 --> 20:15.462
So Clover's first livestream will
be my solo floor boss battle?

20:15.462 --> 20:17.892
Hang on, is that okay with you guys?

20:17.892 --> 20:21.442
Wouldn't it be better if
it involved all four of us?

20:21.442 --> 20:22.402
It's fine!

20:22.402 --> 20:23.082
Yeah.

20:23.082 --> 20:24.292
I don't mind.

20:24.292 --> 20:25.942
Really?

20:25.942 --> 20:27.952
Okay. Great Haste!

20:28.442 --> 20:29.682
Blink Shadow!

20:30.502 --> 20:31.822
Protector Shield!

20:32.651 --> 20:33.901
(Blink Shadow, Protector Shield,
Great Haste)

20:34.532 --> 20:35.652
Begin streaming.

20:36.432 --> 20:37.662
Understood.

20:41.392 --> 20:43.662
Okay, let's have fun, but be careful.

20:46.542 --> 20:50.172
(Steel Crab)

20:58.852 --> 20:59.852
Paralyze!

20:59.852 --> 21:03.102
Slow! Venom! Collapse! Blindness!

21:03.103 --> 21:07.601
(Paralyze, Slow, Venom,
Collapse, Blindness)

21:07.602 --> 21:08.562
Wow...

21:08.562 --> 21:10.862
He used five spells all at once...

21:12.762 --> 21:15.822
That won't work.
I know you're already blind.

21:16.852 --> 21:18.112
Gravity!

21:18.782 --> 21:20.372
(Gravity)

21:28.952 --> 21:31.282
And he's down.

21:31.282 --> 21:33.842
Thank you for watching.

21:33.842 --> 21:35.782
That's the end of this stream.

21:36.502 --> 21:37.172
How was that?

21:37.172 --> 21:38.682
Incredible!

21:38.682 --> 21:40.242
You're amazing, Yuke!

21:40.242 --> 21:42.852
I never knew it was possible
to fight that way!

21:42.852 --> 21:47.102
I can't believe you brought down a
floor boss using only weakening magic.

21:47.102 --> 21:49.882
You cast spells back-to-back.

21:49.882 --> 21:52.772
Quick casts without incantations, even!

21:52.772 --> 21:55.482
I've never seen anything so amazing!

21:55.802 --> 21:58.382
P-Pretty cool, right?

21:58.382 --> 22:00.362
Yeah! It was incredibly awesome!

22:00.702 --> 22:03.292
Marina, you're hurting Master.

22:03.292 --> 22:05.602
Oh! Sorry, Yuke.

22:06.372 --> 22:09.792
One this big should fetch a high price.

22:09.792 --> 22:11.922
We'll let the guild take it apart.

22:12.302 --> 22:14.542
I'll just put it in here, and...

22:16.872 --> 22:19.522
That Magic Bag sure is handy, huh?

22:19.522 --> 22:23.302
But can we really keep depending
on you for everything?

22:23.602 --> 22:26.282
We'll all do the next one together, then.

22:26.282 --> 22:29.812
Not every challenge will work
out as well as this one did.

22:30.102 --> 22:32.692
Yes! You're right, Master!

22:33.102 --> 22:35.322
Well, ready to open that?

22:35.322 --> 22:37.322
A chest!

22:37.912 --> 22:40.032
I wonder what's inside!

22:40.032 --> 22:42.252
Okay, let's all open it together.

22:42.252 --> 22:44.202
Ready, and...

22:46.432 --> 22:47.652
This is...

22:47.652 --> 22:50.642
So Clover has completed its first quest.

22:50.642 --> 22:52.002
Yay!

22:52.002 --> 22:53.732
Today we celebrate!

22:53.732 --> 22:54.622
Good idea!

22:54.622 --> 22:55.990
I agree!

22:56.002 --> 22:58.702
(A Forest Inhabited by Magic Beasts)
Next time, "A Forest Inhabited by Magic Beasts."

22:58.702 --> 23:00.990
(A Forest Inhabited by Magic Beasts)
